  "notes": "Model rate card, USD per 1000 tokens (= the published $/MTok / 1000). Resync-delivered to .loom/pricing.json so a price change reaches the fleet without a Loom release (#8177, ask 2 of #8060). loom-daemon falls back to the compiled card in loom-daemon/src/activity/resource_usage.rs when this file is absent or fails validation, and the two are held in agreement by the shipped_pricing_asset_agrees_with_the_compiled_card test. Rows are an ORDERED cascade: the first row with a `match` substring contained in the (lowercased, alias-resolved) model id wins, exactly like the compiled card. Keep the trailing `claude-<family>-` catch-all of each family pointing at that family's NEWEST published row — an unrecognized id is far likelier to be newer than the card than to be a resurrected retired model.",
